{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5mgwez6sd3vAYKmBT5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `sqlmigrate` now wraps its output in BEGIN/COMMIT only when the migration is atomic **and** the database can roll back DDL. That's the same check the migration executor already uses.\n\nThe change is one line in `django/core/management/commands/sqlmigrate.py`:\n\n```python\nself.output_transaction = migration.atomic and connection.features.can_rollback_ddl\n```\n\nI also updated the comment above it to match. The existing `migrations.test_commands` suite passes (88 tests). I didn't add the new test the issue suggests (mocking `can_rollback_ddl` to False), because the rules say not to edit test files. That means nothing in the existing tests checks the new behaviour."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157,"cache_read_input_tokens":19085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":157},"output_tokens":234,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef466ab7-fb81-45e9-aab0-8e939bc39b5d","uuid":"b030b142-26c7-470d-b978-9c8ca713dec6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:37:38.319Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5mgoiX3MuNZDNj1K7n"}
